meta {
  name: Record the day
  type: http
  seq: 14
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/attendance/days
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "student_id": "{{studentId}}",
    "section_id": "{{sectionId}}",
    "attendance_date": "2026-11-02",
    "forenoon_status": "present",
    "afternoon_status": "absent",
    "reason_code": "MEDICAL",
    "remarks": "Sent home after lunch with a fever.",
    "source": "manual"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
  res.body.forenoon_status: eq present
  res.body.afternoon_status: eq absent
  res.body.section_id: eq {{sectionId}}
  res.body.academic_session_id: eq {{sessionId}}
}

script:post-response {
  bru.setEnvVar("attendanceDayId", res.body.id);
}

docs {
  201 here, unlike the register: one pupil, one day, one row.

  academic_session_id is not sent. It and the branch are read off the section,
  which is also where the branch for the in-session check comes from - so the
  section is what places a day mark in the calendar, and a pupil moving
  section mid-year moves the branch their days are checked against.

  At least one half is required. Sending only forenoon_status leaves the
  afternoon genuinely unknown rather than defaulting it to present, which is
  the difference between "we did not take an afternoon roll" and "she was
  here".

  Each half sent is checked against the calendar independently, so a day that
  is half open accepts half a mark.
}
